            <div xml:id="d356">

                <pb facs="0564" n="468" sameAs="frus:frus1872p1/pg468"/>

                <head>No. 356.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Fish to Mr. Stevens.</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1871-10-05"><hi rendition="#italic">October</hi> 5,
                        1871</date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 5.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>T: I have received your dispatch, No. 5, of
                    the 8th of August last, and have read with much interest the gratifying
                    statement which it contains of the political prospects of a sister republic. The
                    wish of the President for the future of Paraguay, and that the exactions of the
                    governments of Brazil and the Argentine republic in respect to her nationality
                    and territory may be moderate, will be informally communicated to the
                    representatives of those powers.</p>
                <p>I am, &amp;c, &amp;c,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>HAMILTON FISH.</signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
